    "Wang Xingxing is the chairman and CEO of Hangzhou-based humanoid robot maker Unitree Robotics.",
    "The mogul, who is also the firm's chief technology officer, founded Unitree in 2016 after working briefly for Chinese drone giant DJI.",
    "The company has developed over a dozen models including humanoids and quadruped robot dogs, which it now sells globally.",
    "It raised $905 million in a highly-anticipated initial public offering in August 2026. The company subsequently became China's first humanoid robot maker to go public.",
    "One of its more futuristic products is GD01, an over 3-meter tall, transformable mecha that can carry a human pilot in its cockpit -- with a starting price of $650,000."
